6,A phonological description of Naba | Afrika und Übersee,https://journals.sub.uni-hamburg.de/hup1/afrikaunduebersee/article/view/255,"Dec 31, 2022 · Naba, also known as Bilala, is a Nilo-Saharan (Sara-Bagirmi) language of Chad with about 410,000 speakers from three ethnic groups. This paper gives a basic description of the Naba phonological system, using segmental phonology and lexical phonology approaches.",Naba,Nilo-Saharan
